\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Who is your\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 protagonist}{\f0\fs24\b0 ?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~My protagonist will be Joey, an imaginative boy.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #1.1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Is your protagonist ordinary or extraordinary?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~Ordinary, with extraordinary imagination.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #2:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What is his\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 situation\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 at the beginning of the story?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~He is detached from his reality, he is disconnected from his social circle.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #2.1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What is the protagonist\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s personal condition at the beginning?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~He is antisocial, but desires connection}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #2.2:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 How is it going to be changed, for better or worse, by the protagonist himself or by the antagonistic force?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 By him diving into himself, By creating a fantasy world and fantasy friends, he will discover within himself that he cannot make his own connection, he need to connect with others.\~}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #2.3:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Is your protagonist\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s situation ordinary or extraordinary?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 \~Ordinary, everyone experiences this.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #3:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What is the protagonist\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 objective}{\f0\fs24\b0 ?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~External: To defeat the Ice Dragon.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Internal: To open himself and connect with others.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #4:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Who or what is the main\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 opponent}{\f0\fs24\b0 ?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Himself, a part of himself that shuts off from others, a part of himself that is afraid of being ridiculed again.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 That part of himself is personified by the Ice Dragon.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #5:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What early\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 disaster}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~will befall the protagonist and force him out of his \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93normal world\u8221\'94 and into the main conflict?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~He met Chloe. That is a personification of a part of him that desire to be free and adventurous, (note that beyond midpoint, as Joey connects more, he will inhibits Chloe\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s personality)}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #6:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 conflict}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~will result from the hero\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s reaction to the disaster?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~His retreat from the real world and more into his fantasy world. He become more isolated the more he goes to his world for his adventures, thus will be represented by the world getting colder and seemingly the Ice Dragon is winning.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #6.1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What is the logical flow of cause and effect that will allow this conflict to continue throughout the story?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #7:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Is this idea\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 plausible}{\f0\fs24\b0 ?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #8:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Is this idea\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 original}{\f0\fs24\b0 ?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~Inspired by Finding Paradise, Narnia, and Bridge of Terabethia}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #8.1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 How is this idea different from similar stories?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~Because it explore more on the idea of Isolation.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #8.2:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 How can you strengthen its originality?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~By strengthening the Fantasy element more.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #9:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What is the\~}{\f0\fs24\b1 focus}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~of your story?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \~CONNECTION}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #9.1:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 What will be its genre?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Urban Fantasy\~}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Question #9.2:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 Who will be its intended audience?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Young Adults.}}